course: dictionary
lesson: 10921
title: Volleyball in words and numbers
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Volleyball is a team game. Two teams are split by a high net, and players hit the ball with their hands, trying to make it land on the other side.
explain: The word has two meanings: the game and the ball. Read the words around it to tell which one is meant. «A volleyball team has 6 players on the court» is about the team, not the ball.
explain: Maths uses the word too: «27 children: 27 ÷ 6 is 4 with 3 left over, so 4 full volleyball teams, and 3 children keep score.» The sentence tells you one team has 6 players, so you divide by 6 to find how many teams you can make.
fact: Volleyball is a team game played over a high net.
fact: Each team has 6 players on the court.
fact: Beach volleyball is played on sand, with 2 players in each team.
fact: The ball used in the game is also called a volleyball.
fact: Phrases you will meet: play volleyball, a volleyball net, a volleyball court.
exercise: «A volleyball team has 6 players on the court.» How many players from one team are on the court? | 9 | *6 | 4 | 2
exercise: What do players try to do with the ball in volleyball? | Catch it and run away | Kick it into a goal | Hit it into their own net | *Make it land on the other side of the net
exercise: In «27 children: 27 ÷ 6 is 4 with 3 left over», how many full volleyball teams can be made? | 27 | *4 | 3 | 6
test: Beach volleyball is played with how many players in each team? | *2 | 4 | 1 | 6
test: In «Pass me the volleyball», what does volleyball mean? | The court | The net | The score | *The ball
exam: What does the volleyball net do in the game? | Keeps the score for both teams | Holds the ball for the players | *Separates the two teams | Shows where the players sit
